# RustDesk — Speak Friend and Enter

## The Rule
Every gate's RustDesk permanent password IS its gate name in lowercase — same as SSH.

| Gate | IP | RustDesk ID | Password | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| northGate | .147 | 132831540 | `northgate` | ✅ SET |
| eastGate | .244 | 19091278 | `eastgate` | ✅ SET |
| sporeGate | .3 | 1871544996 | `sporegate` | ⚠️ SET (socket warning) |
| ironGate | .237 | (check) | `irongate` | ❌ SSH pubkey-only, no password auth |
| graftGate | .107 | (check) | `graftgate` | ❓ unreachable this session |
| blueGate | .100 | (check) | `bluegate` | ❓ DOWN |

## Config
- Rendezvous + relay: eastGate (.244:21116)
- LAN discovery: ON
- Direct access port: 21118
- Verification: permanent password (not one-time)
- Old public relay (rs-ny.rustdesk.com): removed Nov 14

## SSH Auth Notes
- ironGate only accepts publickey SSH — no gate has the right key
- sporeGate SSH user is `sporegate` (not `root`), needs ProxyJump through eastGate
- eastGate SSH user is `eastgate`, needs sudo for RustDesk admin commands
- eastGate has keys for sporeGate (`id_ed25519`) but NOT for ironGate

## When Adding a New Gate
1. Install RustDesk
2. Set rendezvous: 192.168.4.244
3. Set relay: 192.168.4.244
4. Enable LAN discovery
5. Set permanent password to gate name: `rustdesk --password <gatename>`
6. Enable direct access on port 21118
